WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:04.680
When I first learned about Iran

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:08.420
like most people I was exposed
exclusively to stuff like this:

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:14.679
 

00:00:14.679 --> 00:00:18.260
But as I started to look closer, I started
to see a much different

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:21.730
Iran then what the Islamic Republic
regime represents.

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:25.449
The reaction in Iran to the news about a
potential deal

00:00:25.449 --> 00:00:28.859
is a good example of what I'm talking
about. Immediately following the news

00:00:28.859 --> 00:00:30.189
of this deal with the West,

00:00:30.189 --> 00:00:34.090
people lined up to greet foreign
ministers Zarif as he returned from

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:36.649
Switzerland.

00:00:36.649 --> 00:00:40.840
They spent all night celebrating the
potential lifting of sanctions and

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:44.930
closer ties with the West.

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:49.030
 

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:51.730
So what's going on here?

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:55.270
Is Iran this? Or is it this?   

00:00:55.270 --> 00:00:58.900
A while back I reached out to twenty five Iranians on Facebook.

00:00:59.019 --> 00:01:03.480
These were people between the ages of 21
and 35 who lived all over the country.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:08.060
I started following them and realizing that
they were totally normal people.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:11.830
They posted cat videos and took pictures of 
their food

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:15.869
and talked about clothes and sports and took plenty of selfies.

00:01:15.869 --> 00:01:19.869
I never once saw a dogmatic the
religious posts and I certainly never

00:01:19.869 --> 00:01:26.490
saw anything anti-western

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:30.240
I started to realize that there is a big
difference between what

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:31.189
 I had studied about this regime

00:01:31.189 --> 00:01:36.969
and what the people were actually like.

00:01:36.969 --> 00:01:40.960
These were people who were born after  the 1979 revolution.

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:46.780
They were not a part of the emotion and
their zeal that brought about the

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:49.590
current Iran and all of its hostilities towards the West.

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:53.709
Instead they grew up in an environment of
increase in seclusion from the world

00:01:53.709 --> 00:01:54.200
 

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:58.520
on one hand while gaining huge access to
the world through the internet on the other hand

00:01:58.520 --> 00:01:59.149
 

00:01:59.149 --> 00:02:03.840
So in today's Iran people are less
likely to hate Americans.

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:07.629
In my effort to befriend Iranians on
Facebook,

00:02:07.629 --> 00:02:10.690
I don't have a single person reject my
friend request.

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:14.310
In fact most have them sent me a message
telling me how happy they were to

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:15.010
connect

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:18.250
and how they would love to talk more
about our different cultures.

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:21.670
Politics wasn't a big part of this
conversation.

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:24.799
So, no matter how easy it is to label
Iran is this

00:02:24.799 --> 00:02:28.069
pariah nation bent on hard-line
religious fundamentalism,

00:02:28.069 --> 00:02:32.010
remember that while they're definitely
supporters that ideology,

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:35.519
there is a whole other side to this country
that we rarely see.

00:02:35.519 --> 00:02:39.209
Most Iranians are normal people living
normal lives.

00:02:39.209 --> 00:02:42.349
They want to connect, they want to feel
safe, and

00:02:42.349 --> 00:02:46.609
they want peace as much as you and I do.
That's something I think we can afford

00:02:46.609 --> 00:02:48.450
to talk about a little bit more.

